Interpretation (evidence-backed steps, in order):
- Default Yosys Verilog-2005 frontend rejects the core
  ("unexpected TOK_IMPORT" on package imports).
- With slang, elaboration first failed on 15
  use-before-declaration identifiers in muserisc_core;
  hoisting those six declarations (0b8225b) fixed that
  class. Verilator lint remains clean.
- Next failure class was slang's default unroll limit
  (4000), exhausted by fp_eval (muserisc_fpu_pkg.sv:199)
  and the 512-wide vector loops (muserisc_vec.sv).
- With --unroll-limit=200000, slang canonicalize runs
  13m18s and dies at 7.45 GiB peak (7,626,592 KB),
  i.e. at the local Docker VM ceiling, producing no
  netlist (build/orfs-results/.../base is empty).
  This is a memory-envelope failure of elaborating the
  whole-vector combinational datapath, not a syntax or
  constraint error. No GDS, timing, or area claim for
  the full SoC follows from this run.

